    DR-002 Deferred Recognition Line Views
    =======================================

    Provides list, form, and search views for the ``account.deferred.line``
    model.  Recognition lines are generated by ``account.deferred.schedule``
    records according to the schedule's ``recognition_method``
    (``straight_line``, ``date_based``, or ``manual``) and represent
    individual period-by-period recognition events — one row per recognition
    date per schedule.

    Implements DR-002 acceptance criteria for browsing, filtering, and
    (for draft manual-method schedules) selectively editing recognition
    lines.  The list view is the primary browse interface; the form view
    is mostly read-only after posting; the search view exposes the filters
    accountants use for month-end recognition work (Pending / Posted,
    This Month / Quarter / Year, Overdue Pending, and group-by Schedule /
    Partner / Recognition Month).

    Views registered here:
      1. view_account_deferred_line_tree      (list view — primary browse)
      2. view_account_deferred_line_form      (form view — mostly read-only)
      3. view_account_deferred_line_search    (search view — filters + group-by)
      4. action_account_deferred_line         (window action — menu entry)

    Referenced by:
      - views/menuitem.xml via menu_deferred_line (planned — action_account_deferred_line)
      - views/recognition_dashboard_views.xml drill-down actions (planned)

    Rules compliance (AAP §0.7):
      - R-01 Module Independence: references only ``account.deferred.line``,
        ``account.deferred.schedule``, and core models (``account.move``,
        ``account.move.line``, ``res.partner``, ``res.currency``,
        ``res.company``).  No sibling new-module (``account_budget_management``,
        ``account_asset_management``, ``account_payment_followup``) references.
      - R-02 No Enterprise Dependencies: no Enterprise view/model references.
      - R-03 _inherit Correctness: views target the net-new
        ``account.deferred.line`` model (which uses ``_name`` only, no
        ``_inherit`` on a pre-existing model).
      - R-05 No Core Field Redefinition: declares views for a net-new model
        only; no modification of ``account.move`` / ``account.move.line``
        views here.
      - R-07 No sudo() without justification: no ``sudo()`` in any context
        attribute in this file.

    AAP alignment notes (Odoo 19 conventions):
      - Uses the modern ``<list>`` element (not the legacy ``<tree>``).
      - Uses direct ``invisible="<expr>"`` / ``readonly="<expr>"`` syntax
        (not the legacy ``attrs="{'invisible': [...]}"`` form).
      - Uses ``column_invisible="True"`` to hide the currency column while
        keeping the field available for the monetary widget.
      - Uses ``widget="badge"`` on the state field for colored state rendering.
      - No ``<chatter/>`` on the line form: ``account.deferred.line`` does
        not inherit ``mail.thread`` (only the parent schedule does); adding
        chatter here would fail at install time.
-->
<odoo>

    <!-- =================================================================
         SECTION 1: List (Tree) View — Primary Browsing Interface

         The list view is the default view opened by the menu action.  It
         is optimised for month-end recognition workflows: chronological
         ordering, state colour coding, and a ``Total`` footer on the
         monetary column for quick period-wise reconciliation.
         ================================================================= -->
    <record id="view_account_deferred_line_tree" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">account.deferred.line.list</field>
        <field name="model">account.deferred.line</field>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <list string="Recognition Lines"
                  decoration-info="state == 'draft'"
                  decoration-muted="state == 'posted'"
                  default_order="recognition_date asc, sequence asc, id asc"
                  sample="1">
                <!--
                    Issue #19 fix: shortened column labels (Schedule,
                    Date, Amount, Status, Days) so the list view fits
                    at 1280px without truncation.
                -->
                <!-- Parent schedule reference — always shown, leftmost
                     column for primary identification. -->
                <field name="schedule_id" string="Schedule"/>
                <!-- Partner from the parent schedule (related, stored).
                     Shown by default; can be toggled off via the column
                     picker when not relevant to the user's view. -->
                <field name="partner_id" optional="show"/>
                <!-- The recognition date is the primary chronological key
                     and always visible. -->
                <field name="recognition_date" string="Date"/>
                <!-- Monetary amount with a footer ``sum`` aggregation so
                     users see the total recognition across visible lines. -->
                <field name="recognition_amount"
                       widget="monetary"
                       string="Amount"
                       sum="Total"/>
                <!-- Currency must be in the view for the monetary widget
                     to resolve; ``column_invisible`` hides the column
                     header without removing the field from the record. -->
                <field name="currency_id" column_invisible="True"/>
                <!-- State badge: blue for draft (pending), green for
                     posted (recognized in the ledger). -->
                <field name="state"
                       widget="badge"
                       string="Status"
                       decoration-info="state == 'draft'"
                       decoration-success="state == 'posted'"/>
                <!-- Journal entry reference — hidden by default because
                     most drafts do not yet have a linked move; users can
                     toggle this on when auditing posted lines. -->
                <field name="move_id" optional="hide"/>
                <!-- Audit field: calendar days in the recognition period,
                     used as the proration basis for date-based recognition. -->
                <field name="days_in_period"
                       optional="hide"
                       string="Days"/>
                <!-- Company column hidden by default; only meaningful in
                     multi-company environments. -->
                <field name="company_id"
                       optional="hide"
                       groups="base.group_multi_company"/>
            </list>
        </field>
    </record>

    <!-- =================================================================
         SECTION 2: Form View — Detail Editing (mostly read-only)

         The form shows a single recognition line's full detail.  Because
         recognition lines are generated by the parent schedule's
         allocation algorithm, direct editing is discouraged; the form
         is read-only once the line is posted (``state == 'posted'``) and
         the model-level ``@api.constrains`` enforces the additional rule
         that only ``manual``-method draft schedules allow editing.

         A single smart button links to the posted journal entry when one
         exists; the button is hidden for unposted (draft) lines where
         ``move_id`` is not yet set.
         ================================================================= -->
    <record id="view_account_deferred_line_form" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">account.deferred.line.form</field>
        <field name="model">account.deferred.line</field>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <form string="Recognition Line">
                <!-- =============================================
                     Header — state bar (no workflow buttons; state
                     transitions are driven by the DR-003 cut-off
                     wizard on the parent schedule, not by direct
                     line edits).
                     ============================================= -->
                <header>
                    <field name="state"
                           widget="statusbar"
                           statusbar_visible="draft,posted"/>
                </header>

                <sheet>
                    <!-- =============================================
                         Smart button — Journal Entry drill-through.

                         Bound to ``action_view_move`` on the model
                         (``models/account_deferred_line.py``).  Hidden
                         when no journal entry is linked (``move_id``
                         is unset / False), because there is nothing to
                         drill into.
                         ============================================= -->
                    <div class="oe_button_box" name="button_box">
                        <button name="action_view_move"
                                type="object"
                                class="oe_stat_button"
                                icon="fa-book"
                                invisible="not move_id">
                            <div class="o_field_widget o_stat_info">
                                <span class="o_stat_text">Journal Entry</span>
                            </div>
                        </button>
                    </div>

                    <!-- =============================================
                         Main content — two-column layout.

                         Left column: schedule reference identifies the
                         parent and the partner context; the sequence
                         orders lines sharing the same recognition date.

                         Right column: the recognition plan itself —
                         date, amount, currency, and the audit-trail
                         days-in-period value.
                         ============================================= -->
                    <group>
                        <group string="Schedule Reference">
                            <field name="schedule_id"
                                   readonly="state == 'posted'"
                                   options="{'no_create': True}"/>
                            <!-- Partner is a stored-related field from
                                 the schedule; always read-only on the
                                 line to prevent confusion about which
                                 side of the relation owns the value. -->
                            <field name="partner_id" readonly="1"/>
                            <field name="sequence"
                                   readonly="state == 'posted'"/>
                        </group>
                        <group string="Recognition">
                            <field name="recognition_date"
                                   readonly="state == 'posted'"/>
                            <field name="recognition_amount"
                                   widget="monetary"
                                   readonly="state == 'posted'"/>
                            <!-- Currency shown only in multi-currency
                                 deployments; always read-only because
                                 it is a stored-related value from the
                                 parent schedule. -->
                            <field name="currency_id"
                                   groups="base.group_multi_currency"
                                   options="{'no_create': True}"
                                   readonly="1"/>
                            <!-- Computed audit field; always read-only
                                 (computed on save from the month of the
                                 recognition date). -->
                            <field name="days_in_period" readonly="1"/>
                        </group>
                    </group>

                    <!-- =============================================
                         Accounting Reference group — only visible once
                         a journal entry has been posted and linked.
                         Hidden for draft lines where ``move_id`` is
                         unset to avoid showing empty fields.
                         ============================================= -->
                    <group string="Accounting Reference"
                           invisible="not move_id">
                        <field name="move_id" readonly="1"/>
                        <field name="move_line_ids"
                               widget="many2many_tags"
                               readonly="1"/>
                    </group>

                    <!-- =============================================
                         Company group — multi-company environments only.
                         Always read-only on the line (stored-related
                         from the parent schedule).
                         ============================================= -->
                    <group string="Company"
                           groups="base.group_multi_company">
                        <field name="company_id" readonly="1"/>
                    </group>
                </sheet>
                <!-- Note: no ``<chatter/>`` on this form because the
                     ``account.deferred.line`` model does NOT inherit
                     ``mail.thread`` / ``mail.activity.mixin``.  Audit
                     trail for recognition lines lives on the parent
                     ``account.deferred.schedule`` (which does inherit
                     mail.thread) plus the ``state`` field (tracking
                     opt-in on the model).  -->
            </form>
        </field>
    </record>

    <!-- =================================================================
         SECTION 3: Search View — Filters and Group-By

         The search view provides the filter set accountants use for
         month-end recognition work: find Pending lines due this month,
         group by schedule or partner to see aggregate recognition, drill
         into Overdue pending lines that should have been posted by now,
         and report on annual totals via the year group-by.
         ================================================================= -->
    <record id="view_account_deferred_line_search" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">account.deferred.line.search</field>
        <field name="model">account.deferred.line</field>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <search string="Recognition Lines">
                <!-- =============================================
                     Free-text search fields.
                     ============================================= -->
                <field name="schedule_id" string="Schedule"/>
                <field name="partner_id" string="Partner"/>
                <field name="recognition_date"/>
                <field name="move_id" string="Journal Entry"/>

                <separator/>

                <!-- =============================================
                     State filters — the two primary workflow states.
                     ============================================= -->
                <filter name="filter_pending"
                        string="Pending"
                        domain="[('state', '=', 'draft')]"/>
                <filter name="filter_posted"
                        string="Posted"
                        domain="[('state', '=', 'posted')]"/>

                <separator/>

                <!-- =============================================
                     Period filters — computed from the user's current
                     date via ``context_today()`` + ``relativedelta``,
                     which are both available in Odoo domain eval.

                     The expressions render dates in ISO format so that
                     comparisons against the ``recognition_date`` Date
                     field are lexicographically correct.
                     ============================================= -->
                <filter name="filter_this_month"
                        string="This Month"
                        domain="[('recognition_date', '&gt;=', (context_today()).strftime('%Y-%m-01')),
                                 ('recognition_date', '&lt;', (context_today() + relativedelta(months=1)).strftime('%Y-%m-01'))]"/>
                <filter name="filter_this_quarter"
                        string="This Quarter"
                        domain="[('recognition_date', '&gt;=', (context_today() + relativedelta(months=-((context_today().month - 1) % 3))).strftime('%Y-%m-01')),
                                 ('recognition_date', '&lt;', (context_today() + relativedelta(months=3-((context_today().month - 1) % 3))).strftime('%Y-%m-01'))]"/>
                <filter name="filter_this_year"
                        string="This Year"
                        domain="[('recognition_date', '&gt;=', (context_today()).strftime('%Y-01-01')),
                                 ('recognition_date', '&lt;=', (context_today()).strftime('%Y-12-31'))]"/>
                <!-- Overdue: pending lines whose recognition date has
                     already passed.  These indicate that the schedule's
                     cut-off wizard has not yet been run for the period,
                     or that a manual schedule has lagged behind. -->
                <filter name="filter_overdue"
                        string="Overdue (Pending)"
                        domain="[('state', '=', 'draft'),
                                 ('recognition_date', '&lt;', context_today().strftime('%Y-%m-%d'))]"/>

                <separator/>

                <!-- =============================================
                     Group-By section — the standard axes accountants
                     use to roll up recognition data.

                     In Odoo 19 the ``<group>`` element inside a
                     ``<search>`` view does not accept ``expand`` or
                     ``string`` attributes per the search_view RelaxNG
                     schema (odoo/addons/base/rng/common.rng).  The
                     Odoo UI automatically labels the group section
                     "Group By" based on its position in the search
                     view.  Do not reinstate ``expand="0"`` or
                     ``string="Group By"`` here.
                     ============================================= -->
                <group>
                    <filter name="group_by_schedule"
                            string="Schedule"
                            context="{'group_by': 'schedule_id'}"/>
                    <filter name="group_by_partner"
                            string="Partner"
                            context="{'group_by': 'partner_id'}"/>
                    <filter name="group_by_state"
                            string="Status"
                            context="{'group_by': 'state'}"/>
                    <filter name="group_by_month"
                            string="Recognition Month"
                            context="{'group_by': 'recognition_date:month'}"/>
                    <filter name="group_by_quarter"
                            string="Recognition Quarter"
                            context="{'group_by': 'recognition_date:quarter'}"/>
                    <filter name="group_by_year"
                            string="Recognition Year"
                            context="{'group_by': 'recognition_date:year'}"/>
                    <filter name="group_by_company"
                            string="Company"
                            context="{'group_by': 'company_id'}"
                            groups="base.group_multi_company"/>
                </group>
            </search>
        </field>
    </record>

    <!-- =================================================================
         SECTION 4: Window Action — Primary Entry Point

         Opens the list view by default (list,form) with the Pending
         filter pre-applied — the most common user need is reviewing
         lines not yet recognized in the ledger.

         Referenced by views/menuitem.xml via menu_deferred_line (created
         by the menu-items XML file in the same module).
         ================================================================= -->
    <record id="action_account_deferred_line" model="ir.actions.act_window">
        <field name="name">Recognition Lines</field>
        <field name="res_model">account.deferred.line</field>
        <field name="view_mode">list,form</field>
        <field name="search_view_id" ref="view_account_deferred_line_search"/>
        <field name="context">{'search_default_filter_pending': 1}</field>
        <field name="help" type="html">
            <p class="o_view_nocontent_smiling_face">
                No recognition lines yet!
            </p>
            <p>
                Recognition lines are generated automatically when a
                deferred revenue schedule is confirmed.  They represent
                individual period-by-period recognition events and can
                be posted to the general ledger via the Cut-off Entries
                wizard.
            </p>
            <p>
                Each line records the amount and date of a single
                recognition event; the sum of all lines on a schedule
                equals the total deferred amount, in compliance with
                ASC 606 / IFRS 15 revenue recognition requirements.
            </p>
        </field>
    </record>

</odoo>
